IMPORT prelude

-- Property Tax Act 1960 (Singapore), s 9(2) -- the progressive rates for owner-occupied residential property, set by the
-- Minister's order under s 9(2) instead of the statutory 36% in s 9(1).
--
-- SOURCES. (1) THE ORDER: the Property Tax (Rates for Residential Premises) Order 2013 (S 691/2013), current version as at
-- 11 October 2026, deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PTA1960-S691-2013.txt. It gives the owner-occupier rates from
-- 2025 (Schedule Part 1), the non-owner-occupied rates for 2023 and from 2024 (Part 2), and what counts as owner-occupied
-- (paragraph 4). (2) IRAS, for the EARLIER owner-occupier tables (2015 to 2022, 2023, 2024), which the current version of the
-- Order no longer contains: "Lower property tax rates for owner-occupied residential properties"
-- (https://www.iras.gov.sg/taxes/property-tax/property-owners/property-tax-reliefs/
-- lower-property-tax-rates-for-owner-occupied-residential-properties), read on 10 October 2026. IRAS's 2025 table agrees
-- band for band with Schedule Part 1. The earlier tables were checked only against their own cumulative columns.
--
-- WHY. Added on 11 October 2026 for REQ-0010 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl (cradle-to-grave-simone, event e072: the tax
-- for 2032 on an owner-occupied HDB flat with an annual value of $12,000).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the Comptroller's satisfaction under paragraph 6(2) (an input); paragraph 2(2), the uses that take premises out
-- of "residential premises" (an input); rebates and the s 6(5) $18 floor (ptx-core.l4 has the floor); part-year
-- owner-occupation; years before 2015; paragraph 4(6), (7) (separated spouses, more than one lawful spouse) except as inputs.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human
-- gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Property Tax (Rates for Residential Premises) Order 2013, and the earlier owner-occupier rates as IRAS publishes them`

-- The part of `av` lying between `from` and `to`.
GIVEN av IS A NUMBER, from IS A NUMBER, to IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the slice of` av from to MEANS
    IF av AT MOST from THEN 0
    ELSE IF av AT MOST to THEN av MINUS from ELSE to MINUS from

GIVETH A NUMBER
`no upper limit` MEANS 1000000000000

-- Schedule Part 1, "for the year 2025 and subsequent years" (S 1070/2024 wef 1 January 2025; paragraph 6(1)): "For every
-- dollar of the first $12,000 0%; ... next $28,000 4%; ... next $10,000 6%; ... next $25,000 10%; ... next $10,000 14%; ... next
-- $15,000 20%; ... next $40,000 26%; ... in excess of $140,000 32%". So: 0% on the first $12,000; 4% to $40,000; 6% to $50,000; 10% to $75,000; 14% to $85,000; 20% to
-- $100,000; 26% to $140,000; 32% above.
GIVEN av IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2025 owner-occupier tax` av MEANS
          `the slice of` av 12000 40000 TIMES 0.04
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 40000 50000 TIMES 0.06
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 50000 75000 TIMES 0.10
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 75000 85000 TIMES 0.14
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 85000 100000 TIMES 0.20
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 100000 140000 TIMES 0.26
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 140000 `no upper limit` TIMES 0.32

-- 2024: 0% on the first $8,000; 4% to $30,000; 6% to $40,000; 10% to $55,000; 14% to $70,000; 20% to $85,000; 26% to
-- $100,000; 32% above.
GIVEN av IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2024 owner-occupier tax` av MEANS
          `the slice of` av 8000 30000 TIMES 0.04
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 30000 40000 TIMES 0.06
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 40000 55000 TIMES 0.10
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 55000 70000 TIMES 0.14
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 70000 85000 TIMES 0.20
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 85000 100000 TIMES 0.26
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 100000 `no upper limit` TIMES 0.32

-- 2023: same bands as 2024; 4, 5, 7, 10, 14, 18, 23%.
GIVEN av IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2023 owner-occupier tax` av MEANS
          `the slice of` av 8000 30000 TIMES 0.04
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 30000 40000 TIMES 0.05
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 40000 55000 TIMES 0.07
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 55000 70000 TIMES 0.10
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 70000 85000 TIMES 0.14
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 85000 100000 TIMES 0.18
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 100000 `no upper limit` TIMES 0.23

-- 2015 to 2022: 0% on the first $8,000; 4% to $55,000; 6% to $70,000; 8% to $85,000; 10% to $100,000; 12% to $115,000;
-- 14% to $130,000; 16% above.
GIVEN av IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2015 to 2022 owner-occupier tax` av MEANS
          `the slice of` av 8000 55000 TIMES 0.04
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 55000 70000 TIMES 0.06
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 70000 85000 TIMES 0.08
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 85000 100000 TIMES 0.10
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 100000 115000 TIMES 0.12
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 115000 130000 TIMES 0.14
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 130000 `no upper limit` TIMES 0.16

-- The tax for a year (2015 onwards) on a residential property occupied by its owner for the whole year. From 2025 the Order
-- itself says "2025 and subsequent years"; it can of course be amended.
GIVEN av IS A NUMBER, year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the owner-occupier property tax` av year MEANS
    IF year AT LEAST 2025 THEN `the 2025 owner-occupier tax` av
    ELSE IF year EQUALS 2024 THEN `the 2024 owner-occupier tax` av
         ELSE IF year EQUALS 2023 THEN `the 2023 owner-occupier tax` av
              ELSE `the 2015 to 2022 owner-occupier tax` av

§§ `Schedule Part 2 -- residential premises that are not owner-occupied (paragraph 7)`

-- "For every dollar of the first $30,000: 11% (2023), 12% (2024 and subsequent years); next $15,000: 16%, 20%; next $15,000:
-- 21%, 28%; in excess of $60,000: 27%, 36%."
GIVEN av IS A NUMBER, year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the non-owner-occupied residential tax` av year MEANS
    IF year AT LEAST 2024
    THEN      `the slice of` av 0 30000 TIMES 0.12
         PLUS `the slice of` av 30000 45000 TIMES 0.20
         PLUS `the slice of` av 45000 60000 TIMES 0.28
         PLUS `the slice of` av 60000 `no upper limit` TIMES 0.36
    ELSE      `the slice of` av 0 30000 TIMES 0.11
         PLUS `the slice of` av 30000 45000 TIMES 0.16
         PLUS `the slice of` av 45000 60000 TIMES 0.21
         PLUS `the slice of` av 60000 `no upper limit` TIMES 0.27

§§ `Paragraphs 3, 4 and 6(2) -- when premises are owner-occupied`

-- Para 3: an individual is an owner "if his name appears in the Valuation List as the owner". Para 4(2): premises are
-- owner-occupied "if they are or are to be principally used or occupied as such by the owner". Para 6(2): the Part 1 rates
-- apply only once the owner "satisfies the Comptroller".
-- Para 4(3), (4): on the owner's death the premises stay owner-occupied until the earlier of transfer to the beneficiary (or
-- intestate successor) and 2 years after death, if the Part 1 rates applied immediately before death and the premises are not
-- let in that period.
-- Para 4(5): where a married couple own (together or apart) 2 or more residential premises, ONLY ONE of those they occupy is
-- owner-occupied, "at the option of the Comptroller"; the others are not -- unless (6) they are separated by court order or deed
-- and living apart, or (7) the owner has more than one lawful spouse each occupying different premises.
DECLARE Premises HAS
    `owner named in the Valuation List` IS A BOOLEAN
    `principally occupied by the owner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Comptroller is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
    `chosen by the Comptroller as the couple's one owner-occupied home` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the couple between them own 2 or more residential premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `separated and living apart, or one of several lawful spouses' homes` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN p IS A Premises
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner-occupier rates apply` p IF
        p's `owner named in the Valuation List`
    AND p's `principally occupied by the owner`
    AND p's `the Comptroller is satisfied`
    AND (    NOT p's `the couple between them own 2 or more residential premises`
          OR p's `chosen by the Comptroller as the couple's one owner-occupied home`
          OR p's `separated and living apart, or one of several lawful spouses' homes`)

GIVEN `owner-occupier rates applied just before death` IS A BOOLEAN, `let since death` IS A BOOLEAN, `months since death` IS A NUMBER, `transferred to the beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `still owner-occupied after the owner's death` `owner-occupier rates applied just before death` `let since death` `months since death` `transferred to the beneficiary` IF
        `owner-occupier rates applied just before death`
    AND NOT `let since death`
    AND `months since death` AT MOST 24
    AND NOT `transferred to the beneficiary`

-- The year's tax on residential premises under the Order (from 2023 for the non-owner-occupied rates).
GIVEN av IS A NUMBER, year IS A NUMBER, p IS A Premises
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the residential property tax` av year p MEANS
    IF `the owner-occupier rates apply` p
    THEN `the owner-occupier property tax` av year
    ELSE `the non-owner-occupied residential tax` av year
